        "title": "Avian Evolution: Theropods to Modern Birds",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The origin of birds from theropod dinosaurs is one of the best-documented macroevolutionary transitions in the fossil record. The story went from \"birds evolved from archosaur-like tree-dwelling reptiles\" (Heilmann 1926) to \"birds are living theropod dinosaurs\" (Ostrom 1973 onward), confirmed beyond doubt by the Chinese feathered dinosaur discoveries from 1996 onwards. Modern birds (Neornithes) survived the K-Pg extinction and underwent explosive diversification thereafter."
    },
