      "text": "~240 Mya  ---- Archosauria split: Crocodylomorpha + Avemetatarsalia\n~230 Mya  ---- Early theropods (Eoraptor, Coelophysis)\n~200 Mya  ---- Tetanurae diverge (stiff tails)\n~167 Mya  ---- Paravian theropods (Anchiornis, troodontids, dromaeosaurids)\n~160 Mya  ---- Scansoriopterygidae (tree-climbing; non-bird Avialae)\n~150 Mya  ---- ARCHAEOPTERYX (Bavaria; most famous transitional fossil)\n~130 Mya  ---- Early Cretaceous bird radiation (Confuciusornis, Enantiornithes)\n~130-66   ---- Enantiornithines (dominant Cretaceous birds; ALL extinct at K-Pg)\n~66 Mya   ---- K-Pg extinction: non-avian dinosaurs extinct; most bird lineages extinct\n             NEORNITHES survival: some stem lineages survived\n~66-60    ---- Explosive Neoaves radiation (10-15 Myr window)\n~50 Mya   ---- Modern bird families mostly established\n~34 Mya   ---- Passeriformes diversification begins (Gondwana origin)\nPresent   ---- ~10,600 species recognized\n```"
